>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p>
    I'm Vish. I live in Sydney, work as a senior estimator in retail fitout,
    and spend the rest of my time reading, writing, training, and building
    software I want to exist.
  </p>

  <h2>The professional version</h2>
  <p>
    I price construction work — tenders for shopfitters, fitout contractors,
    retail and hospitality clients. The work is half maths, half judgement, and
    increasingly half AI tooling I'm building myself. See <a href="/work">/work</a>
    for the CV-shaped version.
  </p>

  <h2>The personal version</h2>
  <p>
    I take notes constantly — atomic ideas, things I've changed my mind about,
    lessons from tenders won and lost. The most durable ones land on
    <a href="/notes">/notes</a>. The system underneath is an Obsidian vault
    inspired by <a href="https://stephango.com/">Steph Ango</a>'s file-over-app
    philosophy.
  </p>

  <h2>What I'm trying to do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Get and stay healthy — physical, mental, financial.</li>
    <li>Build a small portfolio of useful software, starting with tools for my own trade.</li>
    <li>Write things I'd want to read if I were ten years younger.</li>
    <li>Own less and read more.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Find me</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Email — <a href="mailto:vishvaddi@gmail.com">vishvaddi@gmail.com</a></li>
    <li>GitHub — <a href="https://github.com/vishvaddi">github.com/vishvaddi</a></li>
  </ul>

  <p style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: #888;">
